id: longevity-supplement
name: Longevity Supplement
kind: gear
craftDC: Expert
# "You can spend 1 Action to consume this item."
placeCost: 1
# "Stop suffering from the Fatigued or Stress Exhaustion Combat Conditions." Both come off,
# every stack: "Conditions", plural, and nothing in the entry asks which.
removes: fatigued, stress-exhaustion
# "You can only use this Basic Item once per Combat Encounter."
oncePerEncounter: true
# Consumed: gone once used.
consumed: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Consume it for an Action to stop being Fatigued or Stress Exhausted. Once per Combat
  Encounter.
text: >
  Longevity Supplement: An aid to health, this item extends your expected lifespan.
  –Craft DC: Expert
  –Effects: You can spend 1 Action to consume this item. If you do, stop suffering from the
  Fatigued or Stress Exhaustion Combat Conditions. You can only use this Basic Item once per
  Combat Encounter.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Consume: 1 Action, and Fatigued and Stress Exhaustion come off, every stack of each. The
# Item is used up - "consume this item" - and taken off the character.
#
# "Once per Combat Encounter" is counted on the character, with the other once-per-Encounter
# uses: two Supplements are still one a Combat Encounter, since the limit is on using "this
# Basic Item" and the second is the same Item. The count clears when an Encounter begins or
# ends.
#
# Not consumed for nothing: with neither Condition on them, the button says so and keeps the
# Supplement.
